revised_prompt:
Convert the following metadata into the canonical format, ensuring comprehensive coverage of all relevant metadata elements.

Canonical format:
{
    "dataset": {
        "name": "",
        "description": ""
    },
    "columns": [
        {
            "name": "",
            "datatype": "",
            "description": "",
            "semantic_type": "",
            "constraints": {
                "nullability": "",
                "length": "",
                "uniqueness": ""
            },
            "comments": ""
        }
    ],
    "primary_keys": [],
    "foreign_keys": [
        {
            "column": "",
            "references_table": "",
            "references_column": ""
        }
    ],
    "relationships": [],
    "lineage": "",
    "ownership": "",
    "profiling": {
        "null_percentage": "",
        "distinct_values": "",
        "value_ranges": ""
    },
    "business_metadata": {}
}

Metadata:
{request}

Ensure to:
- Extract and include data types for all columns.
- Capture primary key and foreign key relationships explicitly.
- Preserve comments, descriptions, lineage, ownership, and profiling data.
- Extract constraint details such as nullability, length, and uniqueness.
- Map source validation rules and enumerations explicitly.
- Handle source variability to maximize metadata completeness.

Return only valid JSON matching the above schema.
